Description:
    Installs RailsEventViewer into your Rails application.

    This will:
    - Create a migration for the events table (if using ActiveRecord adapter)
    - Create an initializer with configuration options
    - Mount the engine in your routes file

Example:
    bin/rails generate rails_event_viewer:install

    This will create:
        db/migrate/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_create_rails_event_viewer_entries.rb
        config/initializers/rails_event_viewer.rb

    And add to config/routes.rb:
        mount RailsEventViewer::Engine, at: "/events"

Options:
    --storage-adapter=ADAPTER  # Storage adapter to use: active_record (default), redis, memory
    --skip-migration           # Skip creating the migration file
    --skip-initializer         # Skip creating the initializer
    --skip-routes              # Skip mounting the engine in routes

Examples:
    # Standard install with ActiveRecord
    bin/rails generate rails_event_viewer:install

    # Install with Redis adapter (no migration needed)
    bin/rails generate rails_event_viewer:install --storage-adapter=redis

    # Only create initializer (skip migration and routes)
    bin/rails generate rails_event_viewer:install --skip-migration --skip-routes
